or if one set has duplicates and the other does not.\n\nTo determine which of the given sets is equivalent to $S,$ we start by listing the elements of $S,$ ignoring any duplicates:\n\n$$\n4,\\,{2,4},\\,2,\\,{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only set equivalent to $S$ is ${2,{2},4,{2,4}}$ since it contains the same elements as $S.$\n\nThe other sets are not equivalent to $S:$\n\n- ${2,4}$ is missing the elements ${2}$ and ${2,4}.$ Note that ${2}\\ne 2.$\n\n- ${2,{2},{4},{2,4}}$ is missing the element $4.$ Note that $4\\ne {4}.$\n\n- ${{2},{2,4}}$ is missing the elements $2$ and $4.$\n\n- ${2,4,{2,4}}$ is missing the element ${2}.$ Note that ${2}\\ne 2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-181636/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d478c5a-3a9e-5219-8111-2cfc828a609a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-181636"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-180827/selection/111c637e86c793ab97de7b59396398d24069e5500dae45b9236f2c4b533b46df" :answer/id #uuid "f3b9461c-9e16-518f-8748-6c32c9708b13" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x,{y},z}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-180827/selection/72c70c16767d6e03e1f569060bb4200a3aea68e57aa50c685b9bb886ef441d5a" :answer/id #uuid "0088216c-eef7-5484-9dca-078769849320" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x,{y},{x,z}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-180827/selection/071cc6c0575672aab26fed2c6b767570bcb30a354cba12dd6344a2db463dc652" :answer/id #uuid "4c19f3eb-6f75-5421-945e-2af4ffd8120e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{{y},z}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-180827/selection/ad3baa539822b41078266ec9f2c22e1825d216f83ed98da00a32703cb2515ef8" :answer/id #uuid "21144741-baf6-5f09-a181-3230b1fdedf6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x,y,{x,z}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-180827/selection/846f21ec61b904680cfe80a72650cdd1d4ecf31aa494f45628e97f04ecc38413" :answer/id #uuid "b52d7c32-ab75-585d-b2a5-e8e223af8e15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{{x},{y},{x,z}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-180827/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "27803171-3b21-5d8a-87ce-046b8d341bee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-180827/selection/72c70c16767d6e03e1f569060bb4200a3aea68e57aa50c685b9bb886ef441d5a" :answer-field/choices ["q-180827/selection/111c637e86c793ab97de7b59396398d24069e5500dae45b9236f2c4b533b46df" "q-180827/selection/72c70c16767d6e03e1f569060bb4200a3aea68e57aa50c685b9bb886ef441d5a" "q-180827/selection/071cc6c0575672aab26fed2c6b767570bcb30a354cba12dd6344a2db463dc652" "q-180827/selection/ad3baa539822b41078266ec9f2c22e1825d216f83ed98da00a32703cb2515ef8" "q-180827/selection/846f21ec61b904680cfe80a72650cdd1d4ecf31aa494f45628e97f04ecc38413"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-180827" :question/id #uuid "a15ebe02-5641-5cee-8a96-d7127c15c7ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-180827" :question/problem "Which set is equivalent to $R={x,{y},{x,z},{y}}?$" :question/worked-solution "Two sets are equivalent if they contain the same elements. It doesn't matter if the elements are listed differently or if one set has duplicates and the other does not.\n\nTo determine which of the given sets is equivalent to $R,$ we start by listing the elements of $R,$ ignoring any duplicates:\n\n$$\nx,\\,{y},\\,{x,z}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only set equivalent to $R$ is ${x,{y},{x,z}}$ since it contains the same elements as $R.$\n\nThe other sets are not equivalent to $R:$\n\n- ${x,{y},z}$ has the element $z$ that is not in $R.$\n\n- ${{x},{y},{x,z}}$ is missing the element $x$ $($note that ${x}\\ne x).$\n\n- ${{y},z}$ has the element $z$ that is not in $R.$\n\n- ${x,y,{x,z}}$ is missing the element ${y}$ $($note that $y\\ne {y}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-180827/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d478c5a-3a9e-5219-8111-2cfc828a609a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-180827"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-183583"] :question/problem "Which of the following intervals is equivalent to ${R}_{0}^{+}?$" :question/worked-solution "The set ${R}_{0}^{+}$ denotes the set of positive real numbers or zero. It is equivalent to the following interval:\n\n$$\n[0,\\infty )\n$$\n\nThe other options are *not* equivalent to ${R}_{0}^{+}:$\n\n- The interval $(-\\infty ,\\infty )$ includes the negative real numbers.\n\n- The interval $(0,\\infty )$ does not include the zero.\n\n- The interval $(-\\infty ,0)$ does not include the positive real numbers or zero.\n\n- The interval $(-\\infty ,0]$ does not include the positive real numbers." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-183591/selection/d6186846956e12d43ab405ff07ff33679fda8e72ed2bc6f020e5b9dd3490e690" :answer/id #uuid "b83d2d10-e7f0-5d85-a6ae-1242d9418b2d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{Q}^{+}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183591/selection/7d512723ec7933fc53d818fe067378407b0cca1985b020babe9fcffa79cfd32b" :answer/id #uuid "86735f26-7761-57b2-99b9-cf115f9e8435" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "Z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183591/selection/1f2752da8d8714b78de92662eac298b0cf876fc7072b0d8faeb2af7d1f2ab6a1" :answer/id #uuid "a6e189ee-4d98-5eed-9fdf-337e24adf1b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{1,2,4,8,16,…}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183591/selection/d602da968f855a4dc10c132bc40dad8d7a6a59db5af85bca8638397d68c46980" :answer/id #uuid "890e9189-69a4-54df-8f22-2fea208db584" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{N}_{0}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183591/selection/c542b243fdeb2d0994ddd0c4e1e11e6e91c124c9ea214587199beb7366e1fe8e" :answer/id #uuid "8ba34747-f690-5b30-9656-f90d0586cb0b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{Z}^{+}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-183591/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ce97527c-c181-5cde-a104-5a5cd55b94c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-183591/selection/c542b243fdeb2d0994ddd0c4e1e11e6e91c124c9ea214587199beb7366e1fe8e" :answer-field/choices ["q-183591/selection/d6186846956e12d43ab405ff07ff33679fda8e72ed2bc6f020e5b9dd3490e690" "q-183591/selection/7d512723ec7933fc53d818fe067378407b0cca1985b020babe9fcffa79cfd32b" "q-183591/selection/1f2752da8d8714b78de92662eac298b0cf876fc7072b0d8faeb2af7d1f2ab6a1" "q-183591/selection/d602da968f855a4dc10c132bc40dad8d7a6a59db5af85bca8638397d68c46980" "q-183591/selection/c542b243fdeb2d0994ddd0c4e1e11e6e91c124c9ea214587199beb7366e1fe8e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-183591" :question/id #uuid "5d5aed40-425c-5f52-a260-d6bf4761a77c" :question/math-academy-id "q-183591" :question/problem "Which of the following sets is equivalent to $N?$" :question/worked-solution "The set $N$ denotes the set of all natural numbers. It is equivalent to the following:\n\n$$\nN={1,2,3,…}={Z}^{+}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${Z}^{+}.$\n\nThe other options are *not* equivalent to $N:$\n\n- The set ${N}_{0}$ includes the element zero, and $0\\notin N.$\n\n- The set $Z$ includes all the negative integers, and $-1\\notin N,-2\\notin N,…\\,.$\n\n- ${Q}^{+}$ is the set of positive rational numbers, and ${Q}^{+}\\ne N.$\n\n- The set ${1,2,4,8,16,…}$ does not include the elements $3,5…$ and $3\\in N,$ $5\\in N,…\\,.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-183591/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e1e872ac-ef9b-50d5-b74f-3f861cdda8f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-183591"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-183585/selection/d887f86454b98c8cce03da5146c8ddbfc0f365883be13302a26376c5df50fe89" :answer/id #uuid "115d289d-6e18-5904-b